# A lowered frame local read in a NUMERIC context while holding a string —
# ouroboros#132.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that aot_lv_num's checked arm had no coverage
# and could be deleted with the whole suite green. t89's first version put an
# unconditional `z is 5` in front of the read, so the slot was ALWAYS numeric
# and the checked arm was structurally unreachable for every input. Replacing
# it with `return 0.0` kept 103/103 passing — while turning a loud death into
# a run-past-error (ouroboros#96), the worst outcome class this repo has:
#
#   VM             Error: cannot apply '*' to str and num          rc=1
#   AOT (checked)  non-numeric value in a numeric context ...      rc=1
#   AOT (gutted)   1                                               rc=0   <- runs past
#
# So the numeric arm lives in t89 and the checked arm lives here, where it is
# the only thing the program does. Both sides must die with the same code.

define numread(k) as:
    local z is 0
    if k > 100:
        z is "big"
    return (z * 2) + 1

print of (numread of 1)
print of (numread of 200)
